---
import ConverterPage from '../components/ConverterPage.astro';
---

<ConverterPage
  path="/kruti-dev-keyboard"
  lede="Which key types which Hindi letter in Kruti Dev 010: consonants, matras, half letters and conjuncts."
  faq={[]}
>
  <h2>Coming in phase 3</h2>
  <p>
    This page will carry the full Kruti Dev 010 layout as a printable chart:
    every consonant, the matras, the half letters, the reph and rakar, and the
    conjuncts that have their own key.
  </p>
  <p>
    The short version, if you need it now: <code>d</code> is
    <strong lang="hi">क</strong>, <code>k</code> is the vertical bar that both
    completes a consonant and serves as <strong lang="hi">ा</strong>,
    <code>f</code> is <strong lang="hi">ि</strong> and is typed
    <em>before</em> its consonant, and <code>Z</code> is the reph, typed
    <em>after</em> the syllable it sits on.
  </p>
</ConverterPage>
